            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Finance of America (FOA): Non-Recurring Gain Drives Profit, Raising Doubts on Core Earnings Quality",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Finance of America Companies (FOA) swung to profitability this year, supported by a higher net profit margin versus the previous period. However, a $54.9 million non-recurring gain clouds the true quality of these earnings. Over the past five years, FOA\u2019s earnings have declined at an average annual rate of 15.6%, while revenue is projected to grow at 8.6% per year, trailing the US market\u2019s 10.5% forecast. Despite the shares trading at just 2x earnings, which represents a sharp discount to...",
